            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-ventura/recipes-phosphor/sensors/dbus-sensors/critical-leak-handler",
                    "line": 94,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Can we at least put this into a function that (by name) documents what the point of this is?  This is a lot of shell script with no description of what it is."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-ventura/recipes-phosphor/sensors/dbus-sensors/critical-leak-handler",
                    "line": 94,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Hsu",
                        "email": "jason-hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "QuantaJasonHsu"
                    },
                    "message": "We have added these change to the function and included comments. Thank you for your suggestion."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-ventura/recipes-phosphor/sensors/dbus-sensors/critical-leak-handler",
                    "line": 98,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "devmem??  Isn't this a GPIO?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-ventura/recipes-phosphor/sensors/dbus-sensors/critical-leak-handler",
                    "line": 98,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Hsu",
                        "email": "jason-hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "QuantaJasonHsu"
                    },
                    "message": "Each SGPIO on the AST2600 has a corresponding memory-mapped register range. In Linux, the register regions of these modules are memory-mapped to physical address ranges via Memory-Mapped I/O. Therefore, by using devmem with the SGPIO address, it's possible to directly access the contents of the corresponding register.\n\nBy using this approach instead of \"gpioget\" command, we can retrieve the SGPIO values even when they are occupied by phosphor-multi-gpio-monitor, without needing to stop the service."
                }
            ],
